<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Byzantine conquest of Bulgaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/968">968</a>–<a href="/years/1018">1018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Byzantine conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> was the series of wars from 968 to 1018 in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John I Tzimiskes</a> took eastern Bulgaria and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a> in 971, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a>, after decades of war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Samuel, won at Kleidion in 1014 and annexed the remaining Bulgarian lands in 1018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/byzantine-conquest-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="Byzantine conquest of Bulgaria" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: from the Middle Ages, unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SamuilsDeathBGhistory.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
